Danielle McGinnis: Um, like, even with Dos Palomas, like, every time they send me an email, they're like, hey, tell me how to do this in the future, which keeps the conversation open for different features they could use.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:50.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. Yeah. No. I think that that that sounds good.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:21:06.000
Whitney Hodges: There was one other thing that I was gonna say, and I feel like I just lost it. Oh, I was gonna say, I feel like with onboarding Tirza, I would just kind of be, like.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:25.000
Whitney Hodges: inquisitive, like, throughout it, right? Of saying, like, is there anything that, like, you typically like to use in GHL that you're, like, not seeing here, or that you, you know, want for Dogwood Reserve, things like that, because she had been unhitched for a really long time, and then she ended up, like, moving over to her own GHL for her account for her venue.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:29.000
Whitney Hodges: So I don't know the extent of what all she…

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:37.000
Whitney Hodges: set up for herself that way. But she's definitely more well-versed than a typical client of, like, what the capabilities are, you know?

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:49.000
Danielle McGinnis: Yeah, and I… I did try to pull some of that out of her, and she was really persistent on just wanting to see what our… she kept calling it our basic package, so I feel like once she's able to see.

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:48.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:21:49.000 --> 00:22:05.000
Danielle McGinnis: like, what we do for Dogwood, then there may be some more flexibility, because we already had reached the understanding that when we get to the end of the asset review piece, I think that's where she's really gonna lay on things that she'd like to see in updates, but right now, when I ask the question, she's just like, oh.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:20.000
Danielle McGinnis: you know, I just want to see what you guys have to offer. Um, and so I think the customization's gonna come at the end when it's time to review the assets. Um, one thing she said she loved was, like, our… the custom Zoom pages and things like that. She thought that was a really nice touch, so…

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:09.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, awesome. Good to hear. Yeah. And then the thing that I feel like we have been now seeing come up repeatedly is the pricing guides and the requests for us to be able to create those, because what we're learning is that, like, when people leave Hitched, technically Hitched, I think, owns the pricing guide or pricing pamphlet.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:53.000
Whitney Hodges: That they call it, which really is, like, a terrible name, um, anyway, in my opinion. So, we've been having to, like, take that pricing, and Giselle's been doing a really good job of, like, turning it into a, um, a Canva design.

00:22:53.000 --> 00:23:11.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, and so, for the time being at least, we'll have Giselle kind of, like, keep doing that piece, at least, like, a really strong first draft, and then she'll share it with, um, Tina, you, and Danielle, and if you guys see that any edits need to be made or anything like that, you can kind of take it from there.

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:26.000
Whitney Hodges: I don't know if you guys think, like… like, at what point in the process you feel like we should be sharing that with them for review? Like, Danielle, if it makes sense to just share that when you're sending all the other assets for them to review, or if that then becomes, like…

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:36.000
Whitney Hodges: them getting more bogged down, you know what I mean? Of, like, do we send separately earlier just the pricing guide for them to approve, sort of thing?

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:34.000
Danielle McGinnis: Hmmm…

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:42.000
Danielle McGinnis: Um, honestly, it doesn't matter to me, because I'm seeing, like.

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:51.000
Danielle McGinnis: I don't typically recommend the onboarding call until they're 100%, like, set on everything that I've sent them, so I feel like if I threw the pricing guide in there.

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:49.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. Mm-hmm.

00:23:51.000 --> 00:24:10.000
Danielle McGinnis: if they have changes, I would just go ahead and forward those to Giselle. I think in the back of my mind, though, I probably would not hold off on the onboarding call pending pricing guide updates, because that would be, like, that's separate from lead lock. Um, but I don't think, like, I don't… I personally don't see why it can't just be put into the asset review email.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:06.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:16.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. Perfect. Yeah. So if you wanna start doing that moving forward, I think that will be great.

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Um…

00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:30.000
Whitney Hodges: I don't know that I necessarily have anything additional that's top of mind for me. I guess I'm curious, probably for you in particular, Felon, because I think it's going to kind of start with you, sort of thing. Um, if you…

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:41.000
Whitney Hodges: feel like you have what you need to kind of, like, dig in and get started, if you feel like you need any more direction or clarity, or if there's anything else I can help with.

00:24:41.000 --> 00:25:02.000
Fallon Looney: No, I think just looking at the like bones of everything inside that sub account is gonna be a good place to start. And I think to your point, it's like the the venues, at least from what I've been finding in these initial audits that I've been doing. It seems like they're.

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:12.000
Fallon Looney: nurture sequence seemed to need the most work. And, like, that part of the wedding is really, like, the non-negotiable, so it's just a little bit different in terms of, like.

00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:07.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:25:12.000 --> 00:25:28.000
Fallon Looney: they have an idea of what they already want, and it's like they're either going to go with the venue, or they're not going to go with the venue. So I think, just looking at it from that lens to your point. I also love like text messages. I know in my.

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:20.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:28.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:47.000
Fallon Looney: experience through the process, like, there's so much noise in the emails, and I think, obviously, we need to have them, but, like, the follow-ups and things that I see there, it's, like, in the back end, like, for views at Sunset Ridge, where we discovered that they have a lot of ad.

00:25:47.000 --> 00:26:05.000
Fallon Looney: Sales, there was a good amount of conversation happening in the text messages from their text follow-ups about going to the tour and like reminding them of the tour where that's where they were getting responses and people were more likely to respond to them of like.

00:25:48.000 --> 00:25:49.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:00.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:13.000
Fallon Looney: oh, I have to cancel the tour, um, we're actually going with another venue. It was, like, a very easy thing for them to then be like.

00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:28.000
Fallon Looney: well, you know, give us any feedback, like, we're excited for you, um, kind of, where did you choose, and why didn't you choose us? And they're much more likely to get that feedback if it comes in a text, I was finding. Um…

00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:18.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:28.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:26:28.000 --> 00:26:29.000
Fallon Looney: So…

00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:34.000
Fallon Looney: Yeah, that's just something like top of mind. But.

00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:36.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:39.000
Fallon Looney: I think I have what I need at least to get started, and I'll let you know if anything comes up.

00:26:37.000 --> 00:27:01.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. Okay. Cool. Yeah, I, I agree. I definitely think the text message stuff we're under utilizing at this point. I mean, it's great that the client can go in and like manually be texting back and forth with people. Um, but like one of the really cool or really good suggestions that I saw from that venue masterclass, and we'll make sure to get y'all that resource was like the pre tour.

00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:16.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, text confirmation, like, not having it just be a confirmation, having it be like, hi, this is Whitney, and, like, including a photo of me, and, like, sharing some, like, tidbits about myself, and saying, this is exactly where I'm gonna meet you on the property, and this is what you need to do when you get here, and, like.

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:36.000
Whitney Hodges: all of, like, a full, like, paragraph about themselves to really kind of build that rapport before they're even, like, walking in the door. Um, but we're also seeing with other, uh, clients who had been utilizing Nurture Pro, um, just even more texts that are being sent out, texts that are including photos, like, hey, like, wanted you to check out this photo of.

00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:45.000
Whitney Hodges: XYZ sort of thing. Um, so all of that could definitely be happening and, um, is not currently happening.

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, where you could probably get a better feel for what has been happening, like, with those other companies. If I'm remembering correctly, Danielle, didn't you, like, opt in for…

00:27:57.000 --> 00:28:07.000
Whitney Hodges: Dos Palomas when they were still with Hitched, and Ridgefield when they were still with NurturePro, and, like, created, like, a doc that, like, basically documented everything that you were receiving.

00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:10.000
Danielle McGinnis: Yep, it's, um, in their client folders.

00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:09.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:22.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, perfect. Yeah, so that'll be, like, a really good way to, like, see what our competitors are actually doing, and how that kind of compares to our… our templates, for sure.

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:30.000
Danielle McGinnis: I think I just had one, um, last question, and it's kind of more around pricing. I think I always get hung up on the non-event workflows.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:31.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:37.000
Danielle McGinnis: Um, so that is always gonna be an additional fee, because it's not included in the initial…

00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:46.000
Danielle McGinnis: like, what comes with their package, right? But, like, for instance, I think you adjusted the price for the ELIA because they had their own copy, is that right?

00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:28:45.000 --> 00:29:02.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm, I did, yeah, and I feel like I've just, like, been case-by-case, kind of, like, charging people different things, or, like, including it for some people, because part of me, like, has felt bad about, like, not, um, setting the right expectations, or, like, foreseeing that.

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:52.000
Danielle McGinnis: Oh.

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:17.000
Whitney Hodges: in the sales process sort of thing. Um, so, I mean, ideally, like, I would like to capture some additional revenue for that, and it seems like we haven't really gotten any pushback, um, when that.

00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:27.000
Whitney Hodges: has come up, but I am also open to, like, as you're kind of working through the proposal and stuff like that, and moving it into GHL, if there's a way where it's just, like.

00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:36.000
Whitney Hodges: an add-on thing that somebody selects, kind of like the pricing guide, right? Like, a way to, like, add that on for an additional $100. Um…

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:43.000
Whitney Hodges: Like, maybe that would be a better way to kind of get in front of it, sort of thing, and actually know that.

00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:49.000
Whitney Hodges: That's going to be part of the scope before that first call even happens.

00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:56.000
Whitney Hodges: But yeah, I mean, I think there is area of opportunity, too, in the venue demo subaccount.

00:29:56.000 --> 00:30:07.000
Whitney Hodges: To potentially already have some templates there, some, uh, calendar funnels, things like that, that are for the, like, non-weddings side of the business.

00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:11.000
Danielle McGinnis: Yeah, because I'm seeing that, like, almost every time now.

00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:12.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. Mm-hmm.

00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:28.000
Danielle McGinnis: Um, and it's basically because the… like… like, I make sure I tell them that it's not included, because usually when we get to the inquiry form, it's like, okay, well, if they select wedding, this is the… this is the path they go down, but if they select any of these other things, like, there's nothing attached to that, and so…

00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:21.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:24.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:28.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:39.000
Danielle McGinnis: because I usually cover it every time, that all almost always comes up. So, I feel like that's why I wanted to get clarity on it, like, is the price different from if they… because some…

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:34.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:45.000
Danielle McGinnis: Here's the difference. Some want to keep the same scheduler, right, but they want a different.

00:30:45.000 --> 00:31:00.000
Danielle McGinnis: they want to use, obviously, different emails that don't reference weddings. Um, we've got some who are, like, like the Ellia, for instance. She had Tina swap out the thank you pages because she doesn't want, you know, the pages to look the same, wedding versus events. Then we have, um…

00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:49.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:30:56.000 --> 00:31:00.000
Whitney Hodges: Wedding pictures, yeah. Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:05.000
Danielle McGinnis: some have their own emails, some do not have their own email, right? So, like, in my mind, I'm… I…

00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:16.000
Danielle McGinnis: each time I bring it up on the call, I find myself saying, I'll get back to you with pricing, which I don't think is awful, but I was just kind of wondering if there would be a way to have, like, something in front of me where I'm.

00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:22.000
Danielle McGinnis: They're asking for non-event, they don't want a scheduler, they have their own emails, but we still have to build it out.

00:31:22.000 --> 00:31:23.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:31:22.000 --> 00:31:27.000
Danielle McGinnis: this would be the price. Okay, they want a scheduler, they want us to write the emails.

00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:39.000
Danielle McGinnis: and they want different thank you pages, it's this price. You know what I mean? Like, so I was kind of just wondering if there was a way to get ahead of that, um, just for the sake of not having to circle back to them.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:31.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:40.000
Whitney Hodges: Right.

00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:49.000
Danielle McGinnis: Um, but it's… no one has, like, given me pushback or anything, I'm kind of just like, hey, it… we don't offer it, but if you'd like, I know we can do it, I just don't know.

00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:47.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, yeah. No, I think we can definitely give you a breakdown of, like, okay, this is what it looks like if they need everything, they need us to do the emails, versus this is what it looks like if…

00:31:57.000 --> 00:32:03.000
Whitney Hodges: they already have their own email copy that they're gonna provide, sort of thing. Um…

00:32:03.000 --> 00:32:10.000
Whitney Hodges: And then that way, you'll kind of know better. But I may toy around with, too, like…

00:32:10.000 --> 00:32:20.000
Whitney Hodges: See, part of me just says, like, oh, well, we just need to include all of that in the foolproof follow-up advantage from the beginning, I need to, like, charge a higher rate, sort of thing.

00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:37.000
Whitney Hodges: But then at the same time, too, I'm like, well, it is nice to be able to just, like, capture people with an easy yes, because the price point is so good, and then, like, upsell them on it later, sort of thing, you know? So it's like, I may have to do some testing on demo calls of, like, okay, if I present all of this.

00:32:37.000 --> 00:32:41.000
Whitney Hodges: And it's a higher price point, like, are they still gonna…

00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:48.000
Whitney Hodges: sign, right? Or are they gonna get sticker shock, or anything like that? So… yeah. That's just kind of where I'm at with it.

00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:53.000
Whitney Hodges: But we'll definitely get you what the upsell pricing is in the meantime.

00:32:55.000 --> 00:32:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:32:56.000 --> 00:32:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Perfect.

00:32:58.000 --> 00:33:02.000
Whitney Hodges: Well, thank y'all for everything. I'm excited to see this come together.

00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:08.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, just let me know if any questions come up. I hope everybody has a good rest of their day.

